WEBVTT

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.700
No one's going to help her?!

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.620
Yuzu could be suffering at this very moment.

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:23.770
She could be injured, waiting to be saved.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.970
Losers are abandoned.

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:28.570
You want to say something, right?

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:30.730
Win the duel and say it to the spectators!

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:35.240
It's the second match of the Friendship 
Cup's second round.

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:40.200
I was distracted by my desire to help 
Yuzu, and Shinji cornered me.

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:43.790
Sora?

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:49.240
That's Yuzu's...

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:53.000
Yuzu... Yuzu's okay?

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:57.840
The real match starts now!

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.100
Getting serious now? But it's too late.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:02.570
I'm not alone.

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:07.550
I have the will of thousands and thousands 
of Commons behind me.

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:10.120
The revolution has already started!

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:13.520
No one can stop us now!

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.540
D-Wheels.

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:21.770
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:23.450
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:26.880
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:29.030
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:07.970
The Awakening Paladin

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:15.100
I activate my spell card Revival Swarm.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:23.900
I can Special Summon one Battlewasp from 
the graveyard, with its effect negated.

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:26.750
Now, Commons, rise up...

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:29.650
It's time for us to come together!

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:31.800
Incite a revolution!

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:33.760
Tear down the Tops.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:37.600
Show them the same suffering 
that we have felt!

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:41.430
I told you to stop provoking the audience...

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.410
Shinji, I understand how you feel.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:48.270
But hating each other this way 
won't change anything!

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:50.880
In order to change this society,

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:53.260
I will make everyone smile with my duel!

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:54.560
Smile?

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:56.540
We'll only be able to smile

00:03:56.540 --> 00:04:00.750
when we've torn the Tops from 
their position in society!

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:04.260
To see that come to pass, I will 
see this revolution through!

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:13.380
I felt that Shinji's revolution wasn't the only way.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:17.340
That's why I pinned my hopes on Jack.

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:21.080
I thought he would change things.

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:24.520
But he didn't do anything.

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:30.460
He retained his position, drunk on 
the money and cheers...

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:32.480
He became the Tops' dog.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:39.380
Shinji is right.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.160
I activate Pin the Bullseye's effect!

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:46.460
Once per turn, I deal 200 points 
of damage to you.

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:51.240
The three Pin the Bullseyes deal 600 total points!

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:58.780
Shinji's series of attacks puts 
the life gap at 1900 to 3400!

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:00.240
He did it!

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:01.720
Go, Shinji!

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:04.170
Yuya...

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:10.960
He's using effect damage to chip away my life, 
and then Azusa will attack Silver Claw?

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:13.480
You're naïve...

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:16.990
You think I summoned Azusa the Ghost 
Bow with its effect negated

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:19.560
just for something like that?

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:22.880
Level 5 Azusa the Ghost Bow

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.640
tunes my Level 1 Pin the Bullseyes!

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:29.770
That Synchro Monster was a Tuner?

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:38.350
Resonant powers, release the arrow of 
resistance in a blaze of smoky fire.

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:40.420
Synchro Summon!

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:45.100
Level 8 Battlewasp — Hama the Conquering Bow!

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:50.500
2800 attack points?

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:53.730
Shinji Weber manages a second Synchro Summon!

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:56.570
Behold, my fellow Commons...

00:05:56.570 --> 00:05:58.940
This is our Synchro Monster.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:04.890
Uniting powerless 200-attack-point monsters 
to summon a monster of revolution...

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:10.480
Now, Commons... Unite around me, 
just like this monster.

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:13.390
We can change this society with our own hands!

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:25.560
Shinji! Shinji!

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:27.190
The feelings of the Commons...

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:29.980
Their rage is uniting.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:36.370
Chairman, at this rate, they really will start a riot.

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:44.550
Shinji! Shinji!

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:47.400
You will not do it.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:50.750
The Tops have oppressed you for all these years

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:53.350
because you are all talk and no action.

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:56.550
That is the nature of the Commons.

00:06:56.550 --> 00:07:00.280
Go ahead, shout and vent your anger.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:03.610
Here I go, Yuya.

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:06.740
I'll defeat you, and stand at the 
vanguard of the revolution!

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:14.810
Hama the Conquering Bow attacks Silver Claw!

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:22.070
Yuya takes 1000 damage! 
He has only 900 life remaining!

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:24.620
Hama the Conquering Bow's effect activates.

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:29.820
Once per turn, I can lower the attack 
points of one of your monsters

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:32.730
by the amount of damage you took!

00:07:32.730 --> 00:07:37.120
And Hama the Conquering Bow 
can attack twice in one turn.

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:40.550
Go, Hama the Conquering Bow...

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:45.060
Attack Timebreaker Magician!

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:49.980
The 1000 damage 
you take will end this!

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:53.210
Is it finished?

00:07:54.230 --> 00:07:55.190
Yuya!

00:07:57.760 --> 00:07:58.840
Yuya...

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:05.500
What is this?

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:08.470
What happened? Why?

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:13.400
I activated Performapal Inflater Tapir's effect.

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:16.030
By sending this card from my hand to my graveyard,

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:18.600
I can reduce damage to 0 once.

00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:23.410
He almost had him!

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:29.420
Yuya...

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:33.160
You won't go down easily, huh?

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:36.910
But your life is down to 900.

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:39.200
I'll finish you off next turn.

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:40.220
I end my turn!

00:08:40.980 --> 00:08:43.740
I can't afford to lose here.

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:49.560
I swore I would use my duel 
to make everyone smile,

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:55.290
end the interdimensional war, and return 
to my world with Yuzu.

00:08:57.100 --> 00:08:58.320
My turn!

00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:03.320
I activate my spell card Match Pump!

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:06.800
I draw one card from my deck.

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:10.590
If that card is a monster of Level 4 
or below, I Special Summon it.

00:09:10.590 --> 00:09:13.400
If it isn't, I banish it.

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:18.390
But if the monster I Special Summon 
is a Pendulum Monster,

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:22.300
that monster is destroyed and 
sent to my Extra Deck.

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:26.380
And this turn, I can't Special Summon monsters 
with any other method than this effect.

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:29.770
If this draw is a Pendulum Monster,

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:34.750
I can use Extra Slinger's Pendulum Effect 
to increase the effect damage I deal.

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:37.990
Draw!

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:39.690
This is...

00:09:40.650 --> 00:09:42.390
Tuning Magician?

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:48.070
What's wrong? Hurry up!

00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:52.400
I Special Summon Tuning 
Magician in defense position!

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:57.980
Tuning Magician?

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:01.770
That's the card I entrusted to Yuya...

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:05.760
I wanted him to win and return it to Jack.

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:08.750
But using that card will be disastrous!

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:12.990
He summoned a Level 1, 0-defense-point monster!

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:17.100
Why does Yuya Sakaki have that card?

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:21.140
When Tuning Magician is Special Summoned,

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:24.040
his opponent recovers 400 life points,

00:10:24.630 --> 00:10:28.240
and he takes 400 damage.

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:29.600
Incredible...

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:34.580
Yuya Sakaki shaved off his own 
life to increase his opponent's!

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:47.610
This is a clear mistake by Yuya!

00:10:47.610 --> 00:10:50.920
The monster effect of the Tuning Magician he drew

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:54.370
makes the life-point differential 3800 to 500!

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:57.600
Why did you put a card like that in your deck?!

00:10:57.600 --> 00:11:01.360
Shaving off your own life, to give 
it to your opponent, is useless.

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:06.040
That's... Tuning Magician is...

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:08.640
If you don't have one, I'll give you this.

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:11.270
This card is the most suited to you.

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:15.350
That was this card?

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:19.720
A low-level monster, with weak attack points.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:22.730
He said it was the monster most suited to me.

00:11:23.190 --> 00:11:26.710
He was looking down on me. Even though 
we're both Commons.

00:11:27.730 --> 00:11:30.940
Why did Yuya put that card in his deck?

00:11:31.720 --> 00:11:35.260
Go, Shinji! Finish him off!

00:11:37.230 --> 00:11:39.310
Looks like it's over...

00:11:39.310 --> 00:11:43.080
The moment you put that useless card 
in your deck, your luck ran out.

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:44.650
That isn't true!

00:11:44.650 --> 00:11:46.550
Every card has a purpose!

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:52.160
I believe that if you accept their feelings, 
the cards will always respond!

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:57.160
I'm using this tournament to prove that.

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:07.100
Tuning Magician...

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:13.080
You can't just exist to hurt the one who uses you.

00:12:16.690 --> 00:12:19.280
I activate Extra Slinger's Pendulum Effect!

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:25.080
For every Pendulum Monster in my Extra Deck, I deal you 300 points of damage!

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:29.930
I have two monsters in my Extra Deck. 
Thus, 600 points of damage!

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:37.040
And now, I can't Pendulum 
Summon again this turn.

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:38.940
I now end my turn!

00:12:39.460 --> 00:12:41.200
Is that it?

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:44.060
You hoped to use that last draw

00:12:44.060 --> 00:12:47.680
to increase the damage Extra Slinger deals.

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:49.930
But you completely missed the mark.

00:12:49.930 --> 00:12:54.230
Drawing that useless card has sealed your fate!

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:56.600
My turn!

00:12:56.600 --> 00:12:59.530
I'll finish off that useless card.

00:12:59.530 --> 00:13:02.890
Hama the Conquering Bow 
attacks Tuning Magician!

00:13:10.300 --> 00:13:11.600
Tuning Magician!

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:13.450
Now, it's over!

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:17.300
Go, Hama the Conquering Bow! Attack directly!

00:13:19.470 --> 00:13:21.650
I activate Gongato's Pendulum Effect!

00:13:22.710 --> 00:13:25.610
Once per turn, if there are 
no monsters on my field,

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:27.610
I can reduce battle damage to 0!

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:32.690
He blocked it!

00:13:32.690 --> 00:13:34.190
It isn't over!

00:13:34.190 --> 00:13:37.530
When Hama the Conquering Bow 
fails to cause battle damage,

00:13:37.530 --> 00:13:43.490
I deal you 300 damage for every 
Battlewasp in my graveyard!

00:13:43.490 --> 00:13:46.300
I have seven Battlewasps in my graveyard.

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:48.730
That's 2100 points of damage!

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:54.450
This time, it's over.

00:13:54.810 --> 00:13:56.910
Go, Hama the Conquering Bow.

00:13:57.210 --> 00:14:00.150
Become the spark that launches 
the signal rocket of revolution...

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:02.890
Yuya Sakaki!

00:14:14.990 --> 00:14:16.300
Yuya!

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:25.810
He dodged it?

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:29.060
I activated my Action Spell Encore.

00:14:29.620 --> 00:14:33.650
I can use this card to activate an 
Action Spell in my graveyard!

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:36.570
An Action Spell in his graveyard...

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:40.680
Yes. I chose Acceleration.

00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:45.230
I used that card to negate Hama the 
Conquering Bow's effect damage!

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:47.970
You're persistent...

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:51.700
But this match is over. Dodging won't save you.

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:55.410
I set one card and end my turn.

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:02.990
I won't let it end like this...

00:15:02.990 --> 00:15:04.430
My turn!

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:08.640
I activate my Continuous Trap Bee Formation!

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:13.610
When monsters on your side of the field 
are summoned or Special Summoned,

00:15:13.610 --> 00:15:16.810
I increase Hama the Conquering 
Bow's attack points by 400!

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:21.720
I don't know what you drew. But every 
time you summon a monster,

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:24.770
this will increase Hama the Conquering 
Bow's attack points.

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:26.700
Shinji seeks to run up the score.

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:29.020
Can Yuya hope to fight back?

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:31.850
Is he finished?

00:15:31.850 --> 00:15:36.230
Clearly, I made too much of him.

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:43.540
Monster Reborn?

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:47.850
A spell card that lets me Special Summon 
a monster in my graveyard.

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:50.230
Right now, in my graveyard, I have...

00:15:55.110 --> 00:15:57.140
I have 500 life left.

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:03.040
Even if I steal Azusa, the monster 
with the highest attack points,

00:16:03.340 --> 00:16:05.630
it won't suffice to stop Hama the Conquering Bow.

00:16:08.770 --> 00:16:10.350
Tuning Magician?

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:39.700
Of course! That's what you wanted!

00:16:40.460 --> 00:16:43.150
I Pendulum Summon with Scale 2 Gongato

00:16:43.150 --> 00:16:46.740
and Scale 6 Extra Slinger already set!

00:16:48.410 --> 00:16:53.240
Be reborn from my Extra Deck, Silver Claw 
and Timebreaker Magician!

00:16:54.410 --> 00:17:00.280
I see... A single Pendulum Summon 
can summon two monsters at once.

00:17:00.280 --> 00:17:03.970
But it doesn't change my attack points' increase.

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:08.950
Bee Formation's effect increases Hama the 
Conquering Bow's attack points by 400!

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:13.410
I activate my spell card Monster Reborn!

00:17:13.910 --> 00:17:16.620
I Special Summon one monster in my graveyard.

00:17:17.110 --> 00:17:20.580
Lend me your aid once more, Tuning Magician!

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:27.640
What, Tuning Magician again?

00:17:27.640 --> 00:17:29.590
What's he thinking?

00:17:31.080 --> 00:17:36.270
Tuning Magician's effect restores 
400 life points to you,

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:39.030
dealing 400 damage to me.

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:42.440
Yuya's life is down to 100...

00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:44.570
Have you gone mad, Yuya?

00:17:44.570 --> 00:17:46.780
Summoning Tuning Magician

00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:50.730
increases Hama the Conquering 
Bow's attack points even more!

00:17:53.180 --> 00:17:55.480
3600 attack points...

00:17:55.480 --> 00:17:57.150
This isn't good at all.

00:17:57.440 --> 00:17:59.620
What's that guy thinking?

00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:02.460
Why did he summon that useless card?

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:07.450
Level 1 Tuning Magician 
tunes Level 4 Silver Claw

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:10.470
and Level 3 Timebreaker Magician!

00:18:10.470 --> 00:18:11.440
What?

00:18:12.780 --> 00:18:15.290
Sword of the hero that puts out gallant light...

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:18.280
Awaken now, in a flash of light!

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:21.210
Synchro Summon!

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:24.720
Level 8 Enlightenment Paladin!

00:18:27.300 --> 00:18:30.790
Yuya just performed a Synchro Summon!

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:34.090
A Pendulum Summon, into a Synchro Summon?

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:35.060
Yuya did that?

00:18:37.110 --> 00:18:40.520
Yuya summoned a Synchro Monster?

00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:43.200
It's too late now.

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:46.970
Hama the Conquering Bow already 
has 3600 attack points.

00:18:46.970 --> 00:18:49.930
Bee Formation's effect increases 
them by another 400!

00:18:54.310 --> 00:18:57.140
I activate Enlightenment Paladin's monster effect!

00:18:57.380 --> 00:19:00.340
When it uses Magicians as Synchro 
Summon components,

00:19:00.340 --> 00:19:03.350
I add one spell card from my 
graveyard to my hand!

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:13.530
What? What's happening?

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:17.340
I add Gap Power from my graveyard to my hand.

00:19:20.690 --> 00:19:21.720
I activate it!

00:19:22.610 --> 00:19:27.680
I increase one monster's attack points by 
half the gap between our life points!

00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:31.760
The difference between our life points is 3500.

00:19:31.760 --> 00:19:36.420
I add half of that value to the attack 
points of Enlightenment Paladin!

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:41.240
4250 attack points?

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:44.060
That's more than Hama the Conquering Bow's!

00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:46.770
All thanks to Tuning Magician.

00:19:46.770 --> 00:19:51.720
Tuning Magician's effect increased 
the difference in our life points.

00:19:51.720 --> 00:19:55.150
Thanks to that, Enlightenment Paladin's attack points

00:19:55.150 --> 00:19:58.140
are higher than Hama the Conquering Bow's!

00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:04.070
You can use the card like that?

00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:09.980
Thanks to Tuning Magician, I was 
also able to Synchro Summon.

00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:13.430
There's no such thing as a useless card!

00:20:13.430 --> 00:20:17.800
If you listen to the cards' feelings, 
they will always respond to you!

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:26.540
Go, Enlightenment Paladin!

00:20:26.540 --> 00:20:28.810
Attack Hama the Conquering Bow!

00:20:54.700 --> 00:20:56.500
Our monster...

00:20:56.800 --> 00:21:00.100
And I activate Enlightenment Paladin's effect!

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:02.700
When it destroys a monster by battle,

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:05.450
it deals that monster's attack points as damage!

00:21:06.260 --> 00:21:08.510
Hama the Conquering Bow's attack points are...

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:10.170
...4000.

00:21:32.400 --> 00:21:34.380
It's finished!

00:21:34.380 --> 00:21:37.890
He turned an insurmountable lead 
into an incredible victory...

00:21:37.890 --> 00:21:40.040
Yuya Sakaki!

00:21:40.750 --> 00:21:43.080
Yuya Sakaki is incredible.

00:21:43.080 --> 00:21:46.320
Thank goodness... For a minute, 
I was really worried.

00:21:59.680 --> 00:22:01.420
Yuya Sakaki...

00:23:49.620 --> 00:23:52.410
Sora! Come out!

00:23:52.410 --> 00:23:53.640
You're there, right?

00:23:53.640 --> 00:23:54.810
Quiet down.

00:23:54.810 --> 00:23:56.190
Come this way. Hurry.

00:23:56.190 --> 00:23:57.320
Sora!

00:23:57.320 --> 00:23:59.290
Yuza's there, right? She's okay, right?

00:23:59.290 --> 00:24:02.990
Yes, I've hidden Yuzu in a safe place.

00:24:03.540 --> 00:24:07.720
I never thought I'd see you here, 
in another dimension.

00:24:07.980 --> 00:24:10.490
After what happened at the battle royal...

00:24:11.200 --> 00:24:14.670
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
A Reunion Across Dimensions.

00:24:15.320 --> 00:24:17.290
The fun is only getting started!
